  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe deadline to file an income tax return is not the same as the deadline to file a protest to an assessment. The income tax return must be filed annually, while a protest against an assessment must be filed within a specific period after the taxpayer receives the assessment notice.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers must be diligent in adhering to both deadlines: they should ensure timely filing of their income tax returns by April 15 each year and be prepared to respond to any assessments by filing a protest within 30 days of receiving the notice. Failure to meet these deadlines can result in penalties or the loss of the right to contest an assessment.",
